{"id":"01a0657e-136c-79fb-8e05-8229aa3956ec","chapterSlug":"rwInterlude - Experiments in Golems","paragraph":546,"wording":"[Golem Artificer]","event":"named","holderSlug":"femithain","holderQuote":"The man flushed with pride and clasped a hand to his chest. Nsiia reflected that Femithain was more bureaucrat and [Golem Artificer] than ruler. But he was not bad at leading men."}
{"id":"01a0657e-136c-70c8-84a1-d9423079e61b","chapterSlug":"rwInterlude - Experiments in Golems","paragraph":607,"wording":"[Golem Artificer]","event":"named"}
{"id":"01a0657e-136c-7789-91df-a690950760e3","chapterSlug":"rw7-48 K","paragraph":220,"wording":"[Golem Artificer]","event":"named","holderQuote":"He’d find himself missing some enchanted stone, a pair of the premade control inscriptions. Bits and pieces he’d never notice; Nsiia carried them off. She was quite smart. It was new to her, but she was feeding off the most accomplished [Golem Artificer] in all of Illivere."}
{"id":"01a0657e-136c-72a0-95df-6106e984a8e7","chapterSlug":"rw7-44","paragraph":225,"wording":"[Golem Artificer]","event":"named","claimed":true,"claimedBySlug":"valeterisa","holderQuote":"Not Zelkyr—but he was a [Golem Artificer]."}
{"id":"01a0657e-136c-7d14-a411-4bc1cb9b1296","chapterSlug":"rw8-12 T","paragraph":1063,"wording":"[Golem Artificer]","event":"named"}
{"id":"01a0657e-136c-76e9-98d8-90c2438c1dfb","chapterSlug":"rw8-15","paragraph":702,"wording":"[Golem Artificer]","event":"named","holderQuote":"Femithain was now the [Golem Artificer] of Illivere, as Domehead had proven. The grand champion of the arena was still smashing heads in, and proving the possibility of creating more Sentient-class Golems at last."}
{"id":"01a0657e-136c-73bb-8ef0-fe8d7523348a","chapterSlug":"rwInterlude - Paradigm Shift (Pt- 2)","paragraph":84,"wording":"[Golem Artificer]","event":"named","holderSlug":"zelkyr","holderQuote":"“Zelkyr was by now an acclaimed [Golem Artificer], and his aspirations were clearly taking him even higher. He desired to create more powerful Golems, even the fabled Sentient-class Golems. It is obvious in journals and notes that his greatest desire was that of a perfect servant. Hence, he would never go anywhere without a personal Golem bodyguard or two.”"}
{"id":"01a0657e-136c-7fe0-a6e5-b2fe79af4b16","chapterSlug":"rwInterlude - Paradigm Shift (Pt- 2)","paragraph":188,"wording":"[Golem Artificer]","event":"named"}
